WEBVTT

00:01.350 --> 00:03.490
A new rival has appeared!

00:03.490 --> 00:05.600
His name is Kojiro Hyuga.

00:05.600 --> 00:08.760
Appearing suddenly during Nankatsu FC's practice,

00:08.760 --> 00:12.070
he displays his overwhelming power to Tsubasa and his friends.

00:12.070 --> 00:15.650
Despite being part of Meiwa FC, Saitama's representatives,

00:15.650 --> 00:18.760
his overly rough play style creates a separation between him and his teammates.

00:18.760 --> 00:21.580
As a result, he leaves his team to fend for itself during the qualifications.

00:21.580 --> 00:25.450
On the other hand, Nankatsu has discovered Wakabayashi's injury.

00:25.450 --> 00:30.170
With worry and anxiety, they enter the prefectural preliminaries.

00:30.710 --> 00:33.880
Due to Tsubasa's efforts, they achieve a magnificent victory.

00:33.880 --> 00:39.500
Nankatsu FC continues to climb the ranks easily after their win.

00:41.670 --> 00:47.730
Now, it's time for the semi-finals match in the Youth Football League's Shizuoka Prefecture.

00:47.730 --> 00:53.730
The second semi-final, Nankatsu FC vs. Shimada Elementary FC, is about to start.

00:53.730 --> 00:57.190
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

00:57.190 --> 01:00.360
Fight! Fight! Shimada!

01:00.360 --> 01:03.370
What? Wakabayashi won't be playing in the match?!

01:03.370 --> 01:05.620
What's the meaning of that, coach?

01:05.620 --> 01:09.620
It seems that Wakabayshi's leg has not completely healed yet.

01:09.620 --> 01:10.790
What...?!

01:10.790 --> 01:17.090
Don't worry. I'm just trying to make sure I can be in tomorrow's match.

01:17.090 --> 01:19.420
Shimada Elementary has no finishers.

01:19.420 --> 01:23.800
There aren't any specific players to worry about, so we can go without Wakabayashi.

01:23.800 --> 01:27.060
You can count on me for the finals, so for today,

01:27.920 --> 01:32.430
I'll leave the goal to you, Morisaki.

01:32.430 --> 01:34.480
Yes. I'll do my best!

01:34.480 --> 01:36.040
Okay, I got it!

01:36.040 --> 01:37.550
We'll show them that we're the stronger team,

01:37.550 --> 01:40.490
even without Wakayabashi playing!

01:40.490 --> 01:42.360
Yeah!

01:42.360 --> 01:45.120
You guys have done well this far.

01:45.120 --> 01:48.030
But, the opponent today is Nankatsu.

01:48.030 --> 01:49.620
They're a powerhouse.

01:49.620 --> 01:50.800
Yes, sir!

01:50.800 --> 01:53.750
There's no need to give up right at the start.

01:53.750 --> 01:59.520
We'll study each and every single play that Nankatsu makes.

01:59.520 --> 02:00.380
Yes, sir!

02:00.380 --> 02:03.050
We'll give it our all!

02:15.080 --> 02:20.710
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

02:15.080 --> 02:20.710
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

02:20.710 --> 02:25.710
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

02:20.710 --> 02:25.710
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

02:26.380 --> 02:31.550
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

02:26.380 --> 02:31.550
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

02:32.260 --> 02:39.890
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

02:32.260 --> 02:39.890
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

02:39.890 --> 02:45.650
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

02:39.890 --> 02:45.650
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:45.650 --> 02:54.160
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:45.650 --> 02:54.160
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:54.160 --> 02:59.960
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:54.160 --> 02:59.960
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:59.960 --> 03:05.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:59.960 --> 03:05.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

03:05.880 --> 03:07.380
<i>Run & Run!</i>

03:07.380 --> 03:14.680
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

03:07.380 --> 03:14.680
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

03:14.680 --> 03:17.600
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

03:14.680 --> 03:17.600
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

03:17.600 --> 03:22.520
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

03:33.690 --> 03:39.100
<b><b>EPISODE 11 :
AN UNEXPECTED STRUGGLE</b></b>

03:33.880 --> 03:36.920
Shizuoka prefecture semi-finals, second game,

03:36.920 --> 03:39.770
Nankatsu FC vs. Shimada Elementary Football Club.

03:39.770 --> 03:43.940
All eyes are on Nankatsu FC, the favorite team to win the preliminaries.

03:44.390 --> 03:48.010
The attack that revolves around the center-forward Tsubasa Ozora

03:48.010 --> 03:53.080
has averaged 9 goals a match. They are the tournament's leading power!

03:53.080 --> 03:59.380
Also, the keeper Wakabayashi has kept a streak of no goals conceded in six matches.

03:59.380 --> 04:03.380
He is not starting this match, due to some issue with his leg.

04:03.380 --> 04:08.260
The starting goalkeeper for this match will be #12, Yuzo Morisaki.

04:08.260 --> 04:11.100
On the other side, Shimada Elementary is a team

04:11.100 --> 04:15.560
that's made it this far through their perseverance, tenacity and hard work.

04:15.560 --> 04:19.330
So far, the first match of the semi-finals was won by the famous Shimizu FC,

04:19.330 --> 04:24.070
with their keeper Kawakami drawing comparisons to Wakabayashi.

04:24.070 --> 04:27.360
Will it be Nankatsu FC or Shimada Elementary

04:27.360 --> 04:29.660
that will go to the finals, victorious?

04:29.660 --> 04:32.510
Wow... so this is Nankatsu?

04:32.510 --> 04:35.050
Everybody looks like they are good at this.

04:35.050 --> 04:36.750
Let's have a good match!

04:36.750 --> 04:38.370
Go easy on us!

04:38.370 --> 04:40.300
What's with these guys?

04:40.300 --> 04:41.880
They're kinda killing the mood.

04:44.130 --> 04:45.420
Hey!

04:48.180 --> 04:49.430
You!

04:50.640 --> 04:53.120
It looks like they aren't very strong!

04:53.120 --> 04:54.720
Hey, Izawa!

04:56.100 --> 04:57.730
What are these guys doing?

04:57.730 --> 04:59.550
Aren't they going to attack?

04:59.550 --> 05:01.690
They aren't pressuring us to take the ball.

05:02.520 --> 05:04.360
Looks like we'll win easily, today.

05:05.280 --> 05:06.280
Go for it, Tsubasa!

05:06.280 --> 05:09.200
Nankatsu's Izawa sends a long pass to the front line!

05:09.200 --> 05:10.320
All right!

05:11.090 --> 05:12.440
It's intercepted!

05:12.440 --> 05:14.990
Izawa's long pass does not connect!

05:14.990 --> 05:16.750
Nice cut, Fujisawa!

05:16.750 --> 05:18.050
Oh, that's bad.

05:18.050 --> 05:19.750
A little obvious, wasn't it?

05:19.750 --> 05:20.920
There!

05:20.920 --> 05:22.410
Fujisawa, the man that stole the ball,

05:22.410 --> 05:23.790
Crap, fall back!

05:22.410 --> 05:25.420
is sending a long pass forward to his teammate.

05:25.420 --> 05:28.170
The ball reaches Nagasaki, Shimada Elementary's captain!

05:28.170 --> 05:29.050
Damn it!

05:29.050 --> 05:32.760
Nankatsu's defense is caught by surprise!

05:32.760 --> 05:34.890
What are you doing, Morisaki?

05:34.890 --> 05:37.020
You're supposed to handle the first line of defense!

05:37.020 --> 05:38.310
Y-Yes!

05:38.310 --> 05:40.720
It's all or nothing!

05:40.720 --> 05:41.400
What!?

05:41.400 --> 05:45.190
Nagasaki unexpectedly fires away at the net from a long distance!

05:45.190 --> 05:46.230
The keeper can't get it!

05:48.820 --> 05:50.200
It's in!

05:50.560 --> 05:54.330
Unbelievable! Shimada Elementary opens up the score!

05:54.330 --> 05:56.330
I did it! It feels to good to be true!

05:56.330 --> 05:59.080
To think we could score against Nankatsu...

05:59.080 --> 06:01.780
Hey! What are you doing, goalkeeper?!

06:01.780 --> 06:04.560
You have to stop those weak shots properly!

06:04.560 --> 06:05.710
Boss!

06:05.710 --> 06:08.280
After a fast counter-attack and long pass,

06:08.280 --> 06:11.130
a long shot from outside the penalty area finds the back of the net!

06:11.130 --> 06:16.870
The streak of no conceded goals by Nankatsu FC has come to an end in the 6th match!

06:16.870 --> 06:18.930
I don't think Nankatsu is very good.

06:21.350 --> 06:22.730
Sorry.

06:22.730 --> 06:25.130
Don't lose heart, Morisaki.

06:25.130 --> 06:28.310
We've scored an average of 9 goals per match.

06:28.310 --> 06:30.780
We'll make a comeback before you can even realize it!

06:30.780 --> 06:31.860
Everybody—

06:31.860 --> 06:35.050
Do you think that we, Nankatsu, will lose in a place like this?!

06:35.050 --> 06:36.990
Let's pick ourselves up and go for it!

06:37.700 --> 06:40.210
Shizuoka prefecture tornament semi-finals.

06:40.210 --> 06:43.250
Nankatsu FC vs. Shimada Elementary.

06:43.250 --> 06:50.050
Nobody could've ever imagined the match would turn out this way...

06:50.640 --> 06:52.550
It looks like it's about to rain...

06:54.360 --> 06:56.300
The first half ends here!

06:56.300 --> 07:00.310
Nanbu FC are comfortable in a three-goal lead!

07:00.310 --> 07:02.390
We're in good shape!

07:02.390 --> 07:03.460
We got this!

07:03.460 --> 07:04.700
This is impossible!

07:04.700 --> 07:08.290
Without Hyuga, reaching the nationals is—

07:09.220 --> 07:10.780
So, is that all you've got?

07:11.400 --> 07:12.710
Hyuga!

07:12.710 --> 07:13.910
Well, what happened?

07:13.910 --> 07:17.160
Weren't you guys gonna win with your football?

07:17.160 --> 07:18.380
Captain...!

07:18.380 --> 07:20.360
Please don't say things like that

07:20.360 --> 07:22.010
and participate in the match!

07:22.010 --> 07:24.830
Please!

07:24.830 --> 07:26.210
Sure.

07:26.210 --> 07:29.800
But... only if you guys play my way.

07:30.480 --> 07:33.300
Hyuga's football...?

07:33.300 --> 07:34.680
That's right!

07:34.680 --> 07:36.970
My style is one that doesn't accept defeat!

07:37.540 --> 07:39.970
Be ready and willing to do anything to win.

07:39.970 --> 07:43.200
It's time for the second half to start.

07:43.200 --> 07:45.980
Meiwa FC will be substituting players.

07:46.740 --> 07:51.320
#10 Hyuga enters, replacing #13 Nakamoto.

07:51.320 --> 07:53.610
What? Hyuga's coming?

07:53.610 --> 07:56.360
He hasn't played in any of these matches. Why now?

07:56.850 --> 08:01.870
#15 Sawada enters, replacing #14 Koyama.

08:01.870 --> 08:04.710
I can play with Hyuga at last!

08:04.710 --> 08:07.910
Captain! Takeshi's still in 4th grade!

08:07.910 --> 08:10.020
Why is he even in this match?!

08:10.020 --> 08:12.250
Watch the second half and find out for yourself.

08:12.250 --> 08:14.720
Takeshi's my partner.

08:15.700 --> 08:17.040
Let's go, Takeshi!

08:17.040 --> 08:18.080
Yes!

08:18.080 --> 08:20.260
The tournament semi-finals,

08:20.630 --> 08:22.880
Meiwa FC vs. Nanbu FC,

08:22.880 --> 08:26.140
the second half to decide the Saitama representative starts now!

08:29.000 --> 08:30.360
Kisugi fires away...!

08:31.270 --> 08:33.700
But the ball goes over the bar!

08:33.700 --> 08:36.610
This is his 10th shot in the first half!

08:36.610 --> 08:37.900
Damn it!

08:37.900 --> 08:40.130
Kisugi, why didn't you pass to Tsubasa,

08:40.130 --> 08:41.550
who was standing right in front of the goal?

08:41.550 --> 08:44.000
I had a chance to shoot! Isn't that fine?

08:44.000 --> 08:46.160
Can you look at the scoreboard and say that?!

08:46.160 --> 08:49.450
We're losing by a point to them!

08:50.910 --> 08:55.740
If you just look at ball possession and shots, we might have the upper hand,

08:55.740 --> 08:58.050
but even then, we haven't been able to score.

08:58.050 --> 09:01.720
What are they doing?

09:03.760 --> 09:07.480
Shimada Elementary counter attacks with another long pass!

09:07.480 --> 09:09.810
Kishida cuts the pass!

09:12.830 --> 09:13.650
Mark him!

09:13.650 --> 09:15.780
This time, we're scoring!

09:15.780 --> 09:17.240
Everybody, mark him!

09:17.240 --> 09:19.030
Yeah!

09:19.030 --> 09:23.120
Shimada Elementary defends against Nankatsu's monstrous attack!

09:23.120 --> 09:25.790
The defense pushes back with force!

09:25.790 --> 09:27.830
The pass is aimed at Kisugi!

09:27.830 --> 09:29.890
It's another long shot!

09:29.890 --> 09:32.840
The ball is safely caught by the goalkeeper!

09:32.840 --> 09:35.200
Is Nankatsu rushing to end things?

09:35.200 --> 09:37.170
They're caught up in Shimada Elementary's defense

09:37.170 --> 09:38.780
and are unable to score!

09:38.780 --> 09:41.010
Why won't they pass to Tsubasa?!

09:42.340 --> 09:44.760
Oh! It's the end of the first half!

09:45.420 --> 09:47.530
In the Shizuoka prefecture semi-finals 2nd match,

09:47.530 --> 09:51.650
Shimada Elementary leads at half-time, 1-0!

09:51.650 --> 09:56.400
Nankatsu FC, the tournament favorites, end the first half without scoring a single goal!

09:58.130 --> 10:00.360
What are you guys doing?!

10:00.360 --> 10:03.420
Your attacking rhythm is all over the place!

10:03.420 --> 10:05.620
Why don't you follow Tsubasa's rhythm?

10:05.620 --> 10:09.280
Well, since our passes are connecting easily past them,

10:09.280 --> 10:12.370
we end up shooting by instinct since we can easily dribble past them.

10:13.700 --> 10:18.880
I understand how you feel, but Tsubasa is much stronger than you guys.

10:19.410 --> 10:20.820
Pass more efficiently and

10:20.820 --> 10:22.120
match Tsubasa's pace in the second half.

10:22.120 --> 10:22.830
Got it?

10:22.830 --> 10:23.680
Yes, sir!

10:23.680 --> 10:26.470
Should I go in the second half, coach?

10:26.470 --> 10:27.360
Wha—

10:27.360 --> 10:29.580
No, we'll go just like this.

10:29.580 --> 10:31.240
We're counting on you, Tsubasa!

10:31.240 --> 10:32.040
Yes, sir!

10:36.520 --> 10:38.440
Huh... it's raining!

10:39.640 --> 10:42.200
How many times have we seent his scene so far?

10:42.200 --> 10:44.580
He dribbles past his opponents and

10:44.580 --> 10:46.860
brings the ball up the line!

10:46.860 --> 10:51.710
#15, Takeshi Sawada! He is the youngest player in this tournament!

10:51.710 --> 10:54.210
Was Takeshi this good before?

10:57.800 --> 10:59.040
Hyuga!

10:59.040 --> 11:01.800
Takeshi sends a cross to Hyuga who is in front of the goal!

11:02.410 --> 11:03.130
That's right!

11:03.130 --> 11:05.640
This duo came into the game for the second half,

11:05.640 --> 11:08.970
and Meiwa FC has caught up to the 3 goal lead!

11:08.970 --> 11:10.970
Get Hyuga! Mark him!

11:10.970 --> 11:13.390
We won't let you score anymore!

11:13.390 --> 11:14.480
Hmph!

11:15.600 --> 11:16.900
We got you now!

11:18.870 --> 11:20.280
Hyuga shoots!

11:24.090 --> 11:26.140
The match is over!

11:26.140 --> 11:27.710
4-3!

11:27.710 --> 11:30.860
The team going for Saitama prefecture finals

11:30.860 --> 11:32.290
is Meiwa FC! What a huge comeback!

11:32.770 --> 11:35.640
What a terrific striker he is!

11:35.640 --> 11:38.640
The boy came in during the second half and

11:38.640 --> 11:40.910
scored 4 goals, leading his team to victory.

11:40.910 --> 11:43.050
His name is Kojiro Hyuga!

11:46.880 --> 11:48.930
Misaki steals the ball!

11:48.930 --> 11:53.230
Nankatsu FC's offense hasn't slowed down in this second half!

11:53.230 --> 11:54.690
Send it here, Misaki!

11:57.100 --> 11:57.610
Oops!

11:57.610 --> 12:02.360
I wonder if it's due to the rain, but it looks like they can't play like they were before.

12:03.000 --> 12:06.610
It seems the goddess of luck is finally smiling down on us...!

12:09.490 --> 12:11.410
What happened to you guys?

12:11.410 --> 12:14.190
Shimada Elementary's matches were always close until now.

12:14.190 --> 12:18.330
I really doubt they're strong enough to stop us.

12:18.330 --> 12:22.170
Coach, please show me the data of Shimada Elementary one more time.

12:22.170 --> 12:23.120
Sure.

12:25.290 --> 12:26.930
Wait, this is...!

12:26.930 --> 12:28.670
As expected of Nankatsu!

12:28.670 --> 12:32.010
Even on the soaked pitch, their passes find their mark

12:32.010 --> 12:33.060
All right!

12:34.060 --> 12:37.560
Oh! The ball gets caught in a puddle!

12:39.590 --> 12:41.500
Certainly, all of their matches were close, but...

12:41.500 --> 12:43.360
Shimada Elementary didn't give up any goals

12:43.360 --> 12:45.360
until now, either. Just like us.

12:45.360 --> 12:47.070
What did you just say?

12:47.070 --> 12:50.780
Every match they've let the opponent shoot away, often in the double digits.

12:50.780 --> 12:53.650
Even then, their entire team protects the goal.

12:53.650 --> 12:58.040
When they can secure the ball, they gamble with a long pass to counter.

12:58.630 --> 13:01.710
This is how they've won 'til now.

13:01.710 --> 13:03.750
So you're saying Shimada is...

13:03.750 --> 13:07.260
Yeah, they're a defensive team through and through.

13:07.800 --> 13:09.800
Shimada Elementary counters again with a long pass!

13:09.800 --> 13:11.800
Guys, get back, quickly!

13:13.900 --> 13:15.350
He shoots, unmarked! It's in!

13:18.070 --> 13:21.360
Shimada Elementary gets a precious second goal!

13:23.090 --> 13:24.610
We scored a second one!

13:24.610 --> 13:26.280
We're not dreaming, right?

13:26.280 --> 13:29.780
It's all good. It's our way of football, nothing else.

13:30.470 --> 13:33.840
We've never had any good finishers to begin with.

13:33.840 --> 13:36.040
Our team was never able to score much.

13:36.420 --> 13:39.040
Those kids really thought it through.

13:39.040 --> 13:43.540
"If we can't score, then we just have to stop them from scoring, too," is what they said.

13:43.540 --> 13:46.670
You might call it a passive or half-hearted way of playing...

13:46.670 --> 13:49.740
But, with their diligence and excellent teamwork,

13:49.740 --> 13:53.980
those kids have cultivated their own skills, little by little.

13:53.980 --> 13:59.580
Now, Shimada Elementary's football is trying to shine.

13:59.580 --> 14:01.810
Good, we can win this match.

14:02.410 --> 14:04.320
What an unexpected turn of events!

14:04.800 --> 14:06.000
We're 10 minutes into the second half,

14:06.000 --> 14:10.360
and the favorites, Nankatsu, are behind by 2 goals!

14:13.490 --> 14:15.890
I definitely won't lose!

14:25.010 --> 14:26.610
In the second match of the semi-finals,

14:26.610 --> 14:28.670
less then 15 minutes remain.

14:29.300 --> 14:31.970
Nankatsu FC, the tournament favorites,

14:32.810 --> 14:35.600
are having difficulties again Shimada Elementary's strong defense.

14:35.600 --> 14:36.780
Coach!

14:36.780 --> 14:37.720
Put me in!

14:37.720 --> 14:40.050
I'll block Shimada Elementary's counters

14:40.050 --> 14:43.100
to let us focus on our attacks. I'll...

14:43.100 --> 14:45.190
No, I won't let you play.

14:45.190 --> 14:49.880
Wakabayashi, our goal isn't just to participate in the Nationals.

14:49.880 --> 14:51.950
It's to win the Nationals!

14:51.950 --> 14:54.490
If we can't overcome an ordeal like this one,

14:54.490 --> 14:56.730
we can't possibly keep up in the Nationals

14:56.730 --> 14:59.120
where the competition will be at its peak.

14:59.120 --> 15:02.250
If that's the case, it's better to lose right here and now.

15:02.250 --> 15:03.750
Coach...

15:03.750 --> 15:06.620
Everyone from Shimada Elementary gathers in front of the goal,

15:06.620 --> 15:08.920
and tightens their defense.

15:08.920 --> 15:12.120
Roberto, Tsubasa won't lose, right?

15:12.120 --> 15:14.560
No... I'm not sure this is something that can be done

15:14.560 --> 15:16.710
with Tsubasa's skills alone.

15:16.710 --> 15:17.430
Eh?

15:17.430 --> 15:21.030
Passing the ball around and crushing Shimada Elementary's defenses...

15:21.030 --> 15:23.720
There's nothing wrong with Nankatsu's tactic.

15:23.720 --> 15:26.520
However, the rain is the problem here.

15:27.480 --> 15:31.390
Normally, Nankatsu's better at controlling the ball,

15:31.390 --> 15:34.530
but because of the rain, the speed of their passes and their ability to trap the ball worsens.

15:34.980 --> 15:38.360
You could say there isn't much difference between their skills, now.

15:38.360 --> 15:41.080
If it keeps going like this... Shimada Elementary, who scored first,

15:41.080 --> 15:42.630
has a huge advantage towards winning.

15:42.630 --> 15:43.580
Ah...

15:43.580 --> 15:46.670
Also, there's always someone marking Tsubasa.

15:47.200 --> 15:47.790
So...

15:50.950 --> 15:53.060
Tsubasa creates an opening upon receiving a pass,

15:53.060 --> 15:55.470
and fires away from a difficult position!

15:55.990 --> 15:58.360
It goes right at the goalkeeper!

15:58.360 --> 16:00.220
Wait, he fumbles it!

16:00.220 --> 16:02.980
The ball slips away due to the rain!

16:03.600 --> 16:05.310
Shimada Elementary saves it!

16:05.310 --> 16:07.560
They send this dangerous ball out of play somehow!

16:07.560 --> 16:09.290
Nankatsu can't score!

16:09.290 --> 16:10.540
Well done, Uesugi!

16:10.540 --> 16:11.440
Nice cover!

16:11.440 --> 16:13.940
Even if we get the ball to Tsubasa, we can't score...

16:13.940 --> 16:16.700
Nankatsu's going to lose this match.

16:18.120 --> 16:20.330
The ball flies over to Nankatsu's side.

16:20.330 --> 16:22.490
Even though Nankatsu tries to get back quickly,

16:22.490 --> 16:23.700
their moves are slowed due to the rain

16:23.700 --> 16:26.200
There are less than 8 minutes remaining.

16:26.200 --> 16:27.120
Going to lose?

16:27.120 --> 16:28.920
Is Nankatsu really about to lose?

16:30.360 --> 16:31.380
Tsubasa...

16:31.940 --> 16:34.300
Like we'd ever lose!

16:37.090 --> 16:39.120
Tsubasa demonstrates his fighting spirit!

16:39.120 --> 16:41.320
He takes the ball and dribbles forward!

16:41.320 --> 16:42.570
Stop him!

16:42.570 --> 16:43.970
All we have to do is stop him...

16:45.730 --> 16:48.310
All right, guys! Let's advance while passing the ball around.

16:51.320 --> 16:52.610
Okay, over here!

16:52.610 --> 16:53.610
All right!

16:53.610 --> 16:54.570
Take this!

16:55.160 --> 16:56.070
Tsubasa!

16:56.070 --> 16:58.030
Okay, we'll keep going, too!

16:58.030 --> 16:58.700
Yeah!

16:58.700 --> 17:00.430
Nankatsu keeps the ball in the air

17:00.430 --> 17:03.110
and continues to connect their passes without using the damp field.

17:03.110 --> 17:04.700
What splendid teamwork!

17:04.700 --> 17:07.330
That's right... That's it, Tsubasa!

17:07.860 --> 17:10.840
Your role isn't just to score.

17:10.840 --> 17:12.570
You can also be a playmaker,

17:12.570 --> 17:14.340
and lead the game yourself!

17:14.340 --> 17:19.090
Without Wakabayashi, no one else can lead this game but you!

17:19.090 --> 17:23.100
Led by Tsubasa, Nankatsu has created a gap in front of Shimada's goal!

17:23.600 --> 17:24.720
Tsubasa!

17:29.560 --> 17:32.370
Tsubasa receives the ball with his right foot

17:32.370 --> 17:34.940
and turns his body around! He shoots!

17:35.700 --> 17:36.840
Goal!

17:36.840 --> 17:41.010
He turns Misaki's perfect cross into a magnificent volley shot!

17:41.010 --> 17:42.950
Nankatsu finally scores against Shimada!

17:42.950 --> 17:44.760
That was great, Tsubasa!

17:44.760 --> 17:45.680
All right!

17:45.680 --> 17:47.540
You did it. We need one more goal!

17:47.540 --> 17:48.030
Yeah!

17:48.030 --> 17:50.080
Shimada Elementary's no goal winning streak

17:50.080 --> 17:51.670
ends with this sixth match!

17:51.670 --> 17:53.460
Don't worry, guys!

17:53.460 --> 17:56.120
Will Nankatsu go after the game-tying goal?

17:56.120 --> 17:58.470
Or will Shimada Elementary manage to keep their lead?

17:58.470 --> 18:00.970
Only 5 minutes remain.

18:00.970 --> 18:02.720
Take this Tsubasa!

18:03.880 --> 18:05.770
Misaki!

18:07.100 --> 18:08.480
All right!

18:08.480 --> 18:11.230
Misaki sends a long pass in front of the goal.

18:11.230 --> 18:12.700
Got it!

18:12.700 --> 18:14.230
A mid-air battle in the rain!

18:14.230 --> 18:16.530
Nankatsu's Izawa wins the ball!

18:16.530 --> 18:18.530
Tsubasa dashes in!

18:18.530 --> 18:20.110
A diving header!

18:21.010 --> 18:22.000
Goal!

18:22.000 --> 18:24.030
With only 2 minutes left in the match,

18:24.030 --> 18:27.040
Nankatsu finally scores the game-tying goal!

18:27.040 --> 18:28.790
You did it Tsubasa!

18:32.760 --> 18:35.070
Nankatsu is really strong, after all...

18:35.070 --> 18:36.000
Yeah...

18:36.000 --> 18:39.090
So this is their true power...

18:39.090 --> 18:40.400
What shall we do, guys?

18:40.400 --> 18:42.660
Should we go on the defensive?

18:42.660 --> 18:44.890
It's not like we have a choice, do we?

18:44.890 --> 18:48.940
But, can we really keep Nankatsu's attacks at bay this way?

18:48.940 --> 18:52.140
Well, even if the match ends in a tie, we'll still have extra time.

18:53.860 --> 18:56.110
Guys, how about we attack?

18:56.110 --> 18:56.770
Eh?

18:56.770 --> 19:00.040
Our teamwork being so good has always been our strong point.

19:00.040 --> 19:01.720
Even if we're not great individually,

19:01.720 --> 19:04.030
we've been able to get results when we all work together, haven't we?

19:04.030 --> 19:06.300
Now is the time for us to come together as one,

19:06.300 --> 19:08.040
and aim for Nankatsu's goal!

19:08.040 --> 19:11.830
We have to do this for our coach's sake, and for all the training he's given us!

19:11.830 --> 19:14.580
We'll score a goal all together!

19:14.580 --> 19:15.970
Yeah!

19:17.040 --> 19:21.210
Shimada Elementary, who have defended with dogged determination all game,

19:21.210 --> 19:23.380
come attacking right out of the gate into Nankatu's side!

19:23.780 --> 19:24.800
What?!

19:24.800 --> 19:28.060
Has this surprise attack successfully caught Nankatsu off guard?!

19:28.060 --> 19:31.310
Shimada toys with them with their excellent pass work!

19:31.310 --> 19:32.800
Are you stupid, suddenly? Don't lose your cool!

19:32.800 --> 19:34.690
Mark them individually!

19:34.690 --> 19:35.590
Hey!

19:36.690 --> 19:37.520
Not yet!

19:37.520 --> 19:40.400
Shimada Elementary manages to pick this ball up!

19:40.400 --> 19:43.150
Shimada Elementary is showing their excellent teamwork!

19:43.150 --> 19:45.660
They aren't letting Nankatsu keep up!

19:45.660 --> 19:47.910
Everyone, attack with all we've got!

19:47.910 --> 19:49.410
Yes!

19:49.410 --> 19:51.150
That's a good team.

19:51.150 --> 19:53.910
Yes. Their play is loose and free.

19:53.910 --> 19:56.420
All right! I won't lose either!

19:57.060 --> 19:58.920
Tsubasa recovers the ball!

19:59.380 --> 20:01.510
However, Shimada Elementary follows up again.

20:01.510 --> 20:02.170
Damn it!

20:02.740 --> 20:03.790
That's it!

20:03.790 --> 20:06.180
Protect that ball!

20:06.690 --> 20:09.720
The football you play relies on teamwork.

20:09.720 --> 20:13.730
You help each other and carry the ball to the goal.

20:15.810 --> 20:16.810
Oh no!

20:16.810 --> 20:19.320
It's a cross towards the goal!

20:19.320 --> 20:21.190
Uesugi is unmarked!

20:25.200 --> 20:28.570
The goalkeeper, Morisaki, stops it!

20:29.480 --> 20:30.910
An excellent save!

20:31.490 --> 20:32.500
Morisaki...

20:33.030 --> 20:35.000
I protected our goal, Wakabayashi!

20:35.000 --> 20:37.840
Morisaki kicks the ball far forward!

20:37.840 --> 20:39.590
It's Nankatsu's turn to counter-attack!

20:39.590 --> 20:40.350
Damn it!

20:40.350 --> 20:41.250
Everyone, fall back!

20:41.250 --> 20:43.150
Tsubasa gets the ball!

20:43.150 --> 20:43.710
All right!

20:43.710 --> 20:47.640
Tsubasa dribbles forward in a mad dash! Shimada Elementary can't keep up!

20:48.510 --> 20:50.760
Tsubasa is one-on-one with the goalkeeper!

20:52.790 --> 20:54.270
GOOOOAAAAL!

20:58.300 --> 21:00.570
The whistle blows! The match ends here!

21:02.550 --> 21:04.690
Nankatsu has turned the tables around and won!

21:04.690 --> 21:08.200
Shimada Elementary was certainly persistent, but they ran out of energy in the end.

21:08.670 --> 21:12.400
Nankatsu's eleven are shouting with joy after a hard-earned victory!

21:12.400 --> 21:14.950
They advance to the finals of the Shizuoka Prefecture Tournament.

21:15.570 --> 21:18.800
And with this last goal, Nankatsu's Tsubasa Ozora

21:18.800 --> 21:21.460
scores a hat-trick for the sixth time in a row!

21:22.730 --> 21:23.710
All right.

21:31.860 --> 21:34.720
You did well, boys.

21:35.200 --> 21:37.560
Let's go and line-up.

21:37.560 --> 21:41.460
We gave everything we had against an opponent like Nankatsu.

21:41.460 --> 21:43.930
We can hold our heads high.

21:43.930 --> 21:44.730
Yeah!

21:45.630 --> 21:47.740
Thank you very much!

21:49.610 --> 21:51.230
Good luck in the final.

21:51.780 --> 21:53.590
Let's play again!

21:53.590 --> 21:54.240
Yes!

21:54.240 --> 21:57.900
Go to the Nationals in our stead.

21:57.900 --> 21:59.370
You don't have to tell me twice!

22:00.150 --> 22:04.000
Shimada Elementary Football Club, you have great teamwork.

22:04.000 --> 22:08.840
I feel like I finally understood what we lack at Nankatsu.

22:08.840 --> 22:12.080
Tsubasa, we'll finally be in the finals next.

22:12.080 --> 22:13.100
Yes.

22:13.430 --> 22:16.600
Let's make sure we win, everyone!

22:16.600 --> 22:18.780
Yeah!

22:38.910 --> 22:44.790
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.910 --> 22:44.790
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.790 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.790 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.810
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.810
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:02.270
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:02.270
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:08.400
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:08.400
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.320 --> 23:15.120
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.320 --> 23:15.120
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.120 --> 23:21.160
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.160 --> 23:26.170
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.160 --> 23:26.170
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.460 --> 23:33.340
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.460 --> 23:33.340
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.340 --> 23:39.220
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.220 --> 23:46.110
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.220 --> 23:46.110
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.200 --> 24:00.810
COMING UP, EPISODE 12 :
CRUSHING WAKABAYASHI
